{"level":"info","message":"<h3>Achievements and Work as a Team</h3>\n\n<p><b>Manas Dadheech</b> worked on DCPEXP-107946, focusing on Prod Amp updates and Streaming UI improvements.  </p>\n<p><b>Shiv Shankar Mistry</b> prepared deskcheck screenshots for a pricing update and also worked on accessibility testing for the membership update flow using screen readers. </p>\n<p><b>Tandrima Bhattacharjee</b> resolved tabbing and styling issues related to DCPEXP-108292, prepared for its desk check, and also contributed to a PR (https://github.com/krogertechnology/esperanto/pull/29887).  She collaborated with <b>Shiv</b> on AMP URL modifications and with <b>Narayan</b> on \"update out of free trial\" changes.  </p>\n<p><b>Shivanand Yadav</b> discussed string changes on AMP with <b>Nitish Jain</b> and worked on DCPEXP-106306, focusing on free trial to paid logic updates.</p>\n\n<br>\n\n<h3>Leave and Holiday Information</h3>\n\n<p><b>Diya Khandelwal</b> was on approved casual leave for a full day on 2025-03-04, and 2025-03-05, and 2025-03-03 for traveling to her hometown. </p>\n<p><b>Manas Dadheech</b> was on approved sick leave for a full day on 2025-03-03 due to illness and travel disruptions.</p>\n<p><b>Narayan Shettigar</b> took a full day of approved sick leave on 2025-03-03 due to illness.</p>\n<p><b>Shivanand Yadav</b> was on approved casual leave for a full day on 2025-03-05 for a family function. </p>\n\n\n<br>\n\n<h3>Backlogs and Issues</h3>\n\n<p>No specific backlogs or issues were explicitly reported this week.</p>\n\n<br>\n","service":"summary-service"}
{"level":"info","message":"<h3><b>Achievements and Work as a Team</b></h3>\n\n<b>Manas Dadheech</b> made progress on DCPEXP-107946, focusing on production Amp updates and Streaming UI updates.  He also participated in daily stand-ups.\n\n<br>\n\n<b>Shiv Shankar Mistry</b> prepared deskcheck screenshots for a pricing update and later continued working and testing the accessibility of the membership update flow with a screen reader. He also joined team meetings.\n\n<br>\n\n<b>Tandrima Bhattacharjee</b> successfully fixed tabbing and styling issues related to DCPEXP-108292, prepared for desk checks, participated in daily stand-ups, raised a pull request (https://github.com/krogertechnology/esperanto/pull/29887), assisted Shiv with modifying AMP URLs, coordinated with Narayan regarding updates, and tested voiceover price readouts across all pages.\n\n<br>\n\n<b>Shivanand Yadav</b> discussed string changes on AMP with Nitish and worked on DCPEXP-106306, focusing on updates to the free trial to paid logic.\n\n\n<h3><b>Leave and Holiday Information</b></h3>\n\n<b>Shivanand</b> took a full day leave on 06-Mar-2025.\n\n\n<h3><b>Backlogs and Issues</b></h3>\n\nNo specific backlogs or issues were explicitly mentioned in the provided updates.  However, ongoing work on DCPEXP-107946, DCPEXP-108292, and DCPEXP-106306 suggests that these tasks may have associated challenges or require further effort.  The need for  desk checks for pricing updates and accessibility testing indicates that these areas are still under development.\n","service":"summary-service"}
{"level":"info","message":"<h3><b>Achievements and Work as a Team</b></h3>\n\n<b>Manas Dadheech</b> worked on DCPEXP-107946, focusing on Prod Amp updates and Streaming UI updates.  He also participated in daily stand-ups.\n\n<br>\n\n<b>Shiv Shankar Mistry</b> prepared deskcheck screenshots for a pricing update and continued working on accessibility testing with a screen reader on the membership update flow. He also joined team meetings.\n\n\n<br>\n\n<b>Tandrima Bhattacharjee</b> fixed tabbing and styling issues related to DCPEXP-108292, prepared for desk checks, raised a PR (https://github.com/krogertechnology/esperanto/pull/29887), assisted Shiv with AMP URL modifications, coordinated with Narayan on free trial updates, and conducted daily stand-ups. She also tested voiceover price readouts across various pages.\n\n\n<br>\n\n<b>Shivanand Yadav</b> discussed string changes on AMP with Nitish and worked on DCPEXP-106306, focusing on free trial to paid logic updates.\n\n\n<br>\n\nThe team collaborated effectively, with members assisting each other on various tasks and contributing to progress on multiple tickets.  Daily stand-ups facilitated communication and coordination.\n\n\n<br>\n\n<h3><b>Leave and Holiday Information</b></h3>\n\n<b>Shivanand</b> took a full day of leave on 06-Mar-2025.\n\n\n<br>\n\n<h3><b>Backlogs and Issues</b></h3>\n\nNo specific backlogs or issues were explicitly mentioned in the provided updates. However, ongoing work on tickets like DCPEXP-107946, DCPEXP-108292 and DCPEXP-106306 suggests continuous development and potential for future challenges.  Further information would be needed to comprehensively assess any backlogs or issues.\n","service":"summary-service"}
