{"level":"info","message":"<h3><b>Achievements and Work as a Team</b></h3>\n\nThis week, the team made progress on several key initiatives.  <b>Manas Dadheech</b> worked on DCPEXP-107946, focusing on Prod Amp updates and Streaming UI improvements.  He also participated in daily stand-ups.\n\n<br>\n\n<b>Shiv Shankar Mistry</b> prepared deskcheck screenshots for a pricing update and continued testing accessibility features with a screen reader on the membership update flow.\n\n<br>\n\n<b>Tandrima Bhattacharjee</b> successfully fixed tabbing issues and styling problems related to DCPEXP-108292, prepared for desk checks, and participated in daily stand-ups. She also raised a pull request (https://github.com/krogertechnology/esperanto/pull/29887) and assisted Shiv with AMP URL modifications.  She further collaborated with <b>Narayan Shettigar</b> on the update out of free trial changes.\n\n<br>\n\n<b>Shivanand Yadav</b> had discussions with <b>Nitish Jain</b> regarding string changes on AMP and worked on DCPEXP-106306, focusing on free trial to paid logic updates.\n\n\n<h3><b>Leave and Holiday Information</b></h3>\n\nSeveral team members took leave this week.  <b>Diya Khandelwal</b> was on casual leave for three days (March 3rd, 4th, and 5th) due to travel.  <b>Manas Dadheech</b> took a full day of sick leave on March 3rd.  <b>Narayan Shettigar</b> was also on sick leave for a full day on March 3rd. <b>Shivanand Yadav</b> took a full day of casual leave on March 4th and 5th to attend a family function.\n\n\n<h3><b>Backlogs and Issues</b></h3>\n\nNo significant backlogs or issues were reported this week.  However, ongoing progress on DCPEXP-107946, DCPEXP-106306, and DCPEXP-108292 continues.  The team is actively addressing accessibility concerns related to the membership update flow.\n","service":"summary-service"}
